      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَارِخَةٌ</span></b>  The <i>voice,</i> or <i>cry, of the calling for aid,</i>
or <i>succour.</i> (K.) Hence the saying, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمِعْتُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَارِخَةَ القَوْمِ</span> [<i>I heard the cry of the people,</i> or
<i>party, calling for aid,</i> or <i>succour</i>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
See also 4. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَارِخٌ</span>.

